{
  "name": "Cross-check AI chat answers with an OpenAI, Anthropic and Gemini debate",
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "b0cc89d2-baf0-4bd2-99fe-d31ccafa83a3",
      "name": "Overview",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.stickyNote",
      "position": [
        -1960,
        -420
      ],
      "parameters": {
        "width": 480,
        "height": 1020,
        "content": "## Debate Arena: three AI providers cross-check each other\nDifferent AI providers have different blind spots. This workflow makes them argue before you get an answer.\n\n### How it works\n1. You ask a question in the chat.\n2. The **Debater** (OpenAI by default) writes an answer.\n3. The **Reviewer** (Anthropic by default) checks it and returns a verdict: agree, or a list of concrete objections.\n4. If the Reviewer objects, the Debater revises. This repeats up to `maxRounds` times.\n5. The **Judge** (Google Gemini by default) makes the final call. It approves, or rejects with a short reason and its own corrected answer.\n6. A rejection starts a new cycle with the Judge's feedback, up to `maxCycles` times.\n7. The chat returns the final answer and a note on how it was reached.\n\nNo model has web search, so answers come from model knowledge only.\n\n### Setup\n1. Add a credential to each of the three model nodes: OpenAI, Anthropic and Google Gemini.\n2. Open **Set debate settings** and set `domain`, `maxRounds` and `maxCycles`.\n3. Click **Open chat** and ask a question.\n\n### Customization tips\n- Any chat model works in any role: OpenRouter, Mistral, Groq, Ollama, AWS Bedrock and more. Just swap the model node.\n- Keep the three roles on different providers. That is where the cross-check value comes from.\n- Set `domain` to make the Debater a specialist, for example \"tax law\".\n- Lower `maxRounds` and `maxCycles` to cut cost and response time.\n\n### Need help?\nQuestions or a custom version? Reach me on [LinkedIn](https://www.linkedin.com/in/huseyinhobek/), [X](https://x.com/huseyinhobek_) or [Instagram](https://www.instagram.com/huseyinhobek_/)."
      },
      "typeVersion": 1
    },
    {
      "id": "7a8418e0-b926-46dd-90c5-43827df9b062",
